WEBVTT

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.780
Suwano's on his honeymoon, eh?

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.030
Ms. Ichiko, how are you doing?

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.570
Have you gotten used to living alone?

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.240
Please give my regards to your nurse friend as well.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.170
Like I said, she's not my friend...

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.630
Slippery! So slippery!

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.810
Hey! You got a lotta nerve to think you can just waltz in here and start watching TV!

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.270
I'm talking to you!

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:12.650
You know, if anything you should be thanking me.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:20.070
While I'm here, I'm preventing that annoying habit you have of draining other people's Fortune.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.080
All thanks to this.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.460
Gadget of Misfortune: Energy Barrier Creating Apparatus!

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:33.000
If someone with high Fortune uses this, it will repel nearby Misfortune!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:39.880
Conversely, if someone with high Misfortune uses it, it will return stolen Fortune to its original holders!

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.510
Surely even you feel some remorse about bringing misfo—

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.190
Oh, shi— Huh?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.190
Mommy!

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.570
That's too bad. Unfortunately for you, aside from Suwano there isn't a single person I value.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.530
You think I'd care what happens to a few nobodies?

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.030
Run along back to the flat plains or wherever you came from.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.410
You little...

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.370
Now it's on!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.080
They're not flat plains! It's the Land of Misfortune!

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.460
I'm gonna teach you a lesson, you little punk!

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.630
Just try it!

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:19.050
No guy in the world would mistake those puny mounds for boobs! They're an eyesore!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.970
Your very existence is an eyesore, you stupid whore!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.720
Why don't you just drop dead and make the world a better place?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.890
You think <i>you</i> can talk?!

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:27.640
Wha—

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:28.890
Oh, shit!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.390
Did I go too far?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.320
See ya, old man!

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:39.990
Crap.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.860
I'll get you next time!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.120
Jeez, talk about annoying.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.290
Please cherish your friends.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.210
Never forget that the character for 'person'
represents two people leaning on each other.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:58.170
Well, whatever. She's not my friend anyway.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.300
She's... gonna die.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.390
<i>Speaking of 'friends'...</i>

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:10.680
<i>I know plenty of guys who'd do anything for me.</i>

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.900
<i>And I don't need to be friends with any of those jealous cows.</i>

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.940
<i>What else is left?</i>

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.320
Man, I really want a boyfriend.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.740
High school life without a guy on your arm is barely high school life at all!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.990
<i>That's right! A boyfriend!</i>

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.870
<i>I wouldn't go so far as to say I don't need one, but...</i>

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.500
<i>I wonder what kind of man would suit me?</i>

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.130
<i>Rather than just having a fairytale prince, I was
thinking something more like the seven dwarfs...</i>

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.460
<i>Damn, that surprised me.</i>

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.880
<i>What's this guy doing here?</i>

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.840
<i>Wait a minute, hasn't that guy been sleeping since episode 1?</i>

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.350
<i>I've never even seen his face...</i>

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.190
Wh-What is it?

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.400
Would you like that heated up?

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.360
Huh?

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.910
Would you like chopsticks with that, as well?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:13.160
<i>That kinda went over my head, but I guess a hottie like that could be my prince.</i>

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.960
Now I get it, Suwano!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.840
The character for 'person' really <i>does</i> represent leaning on others!

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.340
He said leaning on <i>each</i> other!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.800
Gadget of Misfortune: Hell Bunny Ears!

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.300
Not only does it let you hear someone's voice from far away,

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.560
you can even hear things they never wanted anyone to know!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.480
Hey, you know...

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.690
What? Where'd he go?!

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.730
Doesn't waste any time, does he?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.410
Huh? Is that is his student card?

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.910
Tsuwabuki Keita... Oh, nice. Looks like he lives pretty close to me.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.500
I can use this!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.250
You brought it all the way here?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.670
What a beautiful, kind young lady.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.340
Won't you stay for dinner?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.170
We look forward to having you in the family!

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.590
What a splendid development!

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.600
Let's turn this slapstick comedy into a love comedy!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.100
Did my Fortune lead me to him?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.520
The world really would be better off without her.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.360
Is this... it?

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.780
This is definitely the right address, but it's a bit different from what I imagined.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.160
Need something?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.410
Huh? Oh, you're from my class.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.710
Ah... What was it again... A... E... U...

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.080
No, was it... Eu... Ou...Ka...

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.290
I'm Sakura Ichiko.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.340
Um.. This is yours, right, Tsuwabuki?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.840
Oh, it is. You came all this way just to return it?

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.760
Sorry about that. Thanks.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.100
No, no, it's totally fine.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:57.100
Uh... I guess it'd be rude not to invite you in...

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.560
Wanna stay for dinner?

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.850
Sure!

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.810
This is it! Looks like I still got it.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.900
Never mind his house, let's get into the action!

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.940
I'm back.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.610
Welcome home!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:14.160
Oh? Keita brought back a girl!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.620
Oh! We have a guest, a guest!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.750
Oh, welcome.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.620
What's going on? How many of them <i>are</i> there?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:27.380
One... two... three... four...

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.300
Let's eat!

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.810
Ryuuta, you got three pieces!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.180
You're only supposed to have two.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.890
Then I guess you'll just get one today, Mika.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.310
Why me?!

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.070
Cut it out, you two! How many times have I told you not to point your chopsticks at people?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.490
We have a guest today!

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.570
I'm sorry, this is all we have.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.620
<i>I'm getting a distinct sense of déjà vu...</i>

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.500
Okay, meeting time!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.160
Let's begin our strategy session!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.420
Having a cute face is a plus, but it's what comes with it that's the problem.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:12.510
I don't want to play the "I love children!" card right now for this guy.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.300
He'll be like "You okay with this?"

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.300
Won't he bring them along everywhere you go?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.310
Imagine being on a date and having one of them go,
"Yay! Let's make this into a picnic!"

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.100
Let's vote.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.060
Rejected!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.440
All right.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.440
Requesting change of course to "rejected!"

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.740
Roger that.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.570
<i>Well, it was a nice dream while it lasted.</i>

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:38.660
B-By the way, where are your parents?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:39.740
They ran away.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:47.130
They got into a lot of debt and said something about going to find the lost treasure of Tokugawa.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.460
They never came back.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.960
Are you serious?

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:56.510
In the end, I had to take on a lot of part-time jobs so I could feed these guys.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.010
And that's why you're always asleep at school?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.720
Yeah, 'cause I can only get night shifts.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:05.480
But when I see these guys, my fatigue just fades away.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.270
What's wrong?

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.280
Being poor doesn't leave you any free time, eh?

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.780
There's no way I could live like that.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.780
Don't say that.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:25.410
We don't have a lot of money, but we're happy together. That's what matters, right?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.500
Happy together, huh?

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.840
But if you had money, you'd be even happier, right?

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:36.050
There are a lot of things more important than money.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.680
Like what?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.600
Why bring that up out of nowhere?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.680
That doesn't answer my question. Tell me what you really think.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:50.940
If you had money, you'd be able to live in a bigger house, and eat better food.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.230
Am I wrong?

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.900
How can you say something like that?

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.950
I don't know if you're just feeling rebellious or
playing devil's advocate or whatever, but stop it!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.700
You sound just like that God of Misfortune!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.870
God of Misfortune?

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.620
Well, then...

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.120
Well then!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.750
How about this? Spend it on anything you like!

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.880
Admit it or not, at the end of the day this is what you need, right?

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.130
Tomorrow, you can eat something ten times as good!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.590
Wow!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.090
How much is this?

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.850
Don't touch it, you two!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.140
I've had enough!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:25.520
Calm down, Rika.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.350
Sorry, Sakura.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.140
Keita!

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:36.400
Maybe I should apologize first. I shouldn't have invited you in to begin with.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.030
Now get out of here!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:46.040
Keita's angry!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.410
That's right!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.880
Do you realize what a terrible thing you've done?!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.210
Shut up, God of Misfortune!

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.420
Shut up.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.420
I'm leaving! You don't have to tell me.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.300
What the fuck was <i>his</i> problem?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.220
Shut up, woman!

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.890
Just wanted to try saying something like he would.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.140
Why're you trying to make <i>me</i> look like the only one at fault?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:15.860
You might look rich, but on the inside you're morally bankrupt, aren't you?

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:16.980
Why, you...

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.320
If you have something to say...

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.660
Say it to my goddamn face!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.490
Not really.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:30.000
I'm just here to fulfill my mission. I don't care about your personality issues.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.620
What the hell?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.960
Why's everyone out to get me?

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.970
Hasn't the weather been a bit unusual?

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.980
I think there's a typhoon on the way.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:52.980
Jeez, I'm still pissed off about yesterday.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.480
It's totally ruining my day off!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.610
Oh, it's that mean girl.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.820
<i>Tsuwabuki's little brother!</i>

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:04.820
It's just like Keita said. "People who only care about money have tiny, shriveled hearts."

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.280
I bet that's why you're so mean.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.410
I have a name, and it's Sakura Ichiko.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.750
Oh, so that's why you have such huge tits.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:17.750
I said Ichiko, not Tittyko, you little brat!

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.210
Oh, I got the same one again.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.260
Hey, if you don't need it, let me have it.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.470
Huh? Why don't you buy your own for once?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.640
Ryuuta, you're always tryin' to mooch off us.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:29.970
Oh! That's it!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:35.480
I'll buy his siblings' affection, then make him apologize and admit the error of his ways!

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:39.020
Okay, okay, I'll buy you a card.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.940
What? I don't want one!

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.440
I just told you I don't want one!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:47.740
Don't worry, it's my treat. If it sucks, you can just toss it.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:50.160
Huh?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.660
Whoa, amazing! That's a super rare card!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.040
He got it first try!

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.580
How's <i>that</i> for lucky?

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.550
You know as well as I do that was thanks to your Fortune!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.510
Um... Th-Thanks.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.890
Not so mean now, am I?

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:13.890
My brother told me to always say thanks
whenever someone gives me something.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.770
No matter how mean they are.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.690
Don't worry about it. It's not a big deal.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.150
Thanks a lot, Tittyko!

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:27.990
You mean "Miss Ichiko," right?

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.620
Dude, that's so cool!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.120
Can I see it again?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.500
I've bought so many of those and never even seen one!

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:40.500
That was a little different to what I had in mind, but I've got a good feeling about this all the same. It'll do.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.960
So even Tittyko's got a good side to her.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:49.970
Oh, but what'll I tell my brother? If I tell him Tittyko bought it, he'll probably get mad...

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.430
Huh? Ah!

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.270
I'm such an idiot!

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.890
Are you serious! You've gotta be kidding me!

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:02.820
Is it even still here? It's dark, and it stinks!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.990
What's this? That's pretty dangerous.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.360
Wonder if they were doing some work in the sewers?

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.370
Thank goodness I found it.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.790
I'll have to clean it up once I get back.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.460
Huh? Why's it... closed?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.000
I'm back.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.550
What's with this rain?

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:28.630
Keita, Ryuu... Ryuu still hasn't come home.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:32.810
I called all his friends, but he's not with any of them.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.430
Seriously?

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.980
Keita... help me!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.980
Ryuu... Ryuuta!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.400
Ryuuta!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.360
<i>Is there anything I haven't thought of yet?</i>

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.160
<i>Anyone else who knows Ryuu?</i>

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:53.950
<i>There's one more person.</i>

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.660
Who the hell'd turn up at this time?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:00.670
Tsuwabuki!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.960
What? You're soaked.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.970
Has Ryuu been by here? My little brother.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.220
Nope.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.550
But if this is about the card, you don't have to pay me back.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.010
Huh? What card?

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.100
Did you buy something for him?

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.520
It's not a big deal.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:19.980
How much?

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.770
Three hundred yen.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.480
Dammit, Ryuu... We're not made of money...

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:31.030
Looks like you have it hard, "big brother".

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:31.490
What?

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:37.870
To be honest, I don't think all the things you said were wrong.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:43.880
Ryuu really wants to play soccer, but we'd have to play for a ball, cleats, and club fees.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.210
So he just plays old video games instead.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:54.680
I want to buy Rika her own desk, and Mika and Sorata some clothes that aren't hand-me-downs.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.350
If we had money, we'd probably take all that happiness for granted,

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.430
but since we have none, I know just how unhappy we are!

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.400
Then just ask someone for help!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.520
I can't do that.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.440
Why?

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:13.820
It might just be my own pointless sense of pride, but being able to stand on my own two feet is what gives me the right to live!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.240
That's the example I want to set for my brothers and sisters!

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.790
At the very least, I refuse to be in your debt!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:31.220
Well? If you want to say something, just say it.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.760
No, nothing in particular.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.220
What is it then?

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:43.730
Wh-What are you doing? What is this?

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.100
Can you hear it?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.020
Huh? Hear what?

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.610
Keita!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:56.410
His little brother's in serious trouble right now.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.120
Huh? No way...

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.670
Ryuu!

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:11.170
By the way, the louder the voice, the closer they are.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.470
What are you trying to make me do?

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.880
Who knows?

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:15.880
But...

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.300
That's...

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:25.770
That's right. What if I told you you could save that boy with your Fortune?

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:31.280
Use your Fortune to help others of your own volition.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.200
Depending on how things turn out, maybe you'll do my job for me.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:43.080
Oh, but that's right. Aside from Suwano, you don't care about happens to a "few nobodies," do you?

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.580
Um... Th-Thanks.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:53.340
I... still don't think I'm wrong.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.720
I won't deny the part about money.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.140
I just want to wipe that proud glare off his face.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.470
Then do it.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.890
I... don't give a shit what happens to a few nobodies!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.350
Then, that boy?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:20.280
Then go. If that boy isn't just a nobody, then go.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.120
Oh yeah, one more thing.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.460
Being ordered around by you somehow makes me really angry!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:32.170
What do you mean 'somehow'?!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:38.430
That... bitch.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.430
She's not honest with herself, is she?

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:45.890
Humans may be overwhelmingly petty creatures,

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.560
but even they have their moments.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:52.190
Ryuu! Where are you?!

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.070
Keita!

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.690
Ryuu! You idiot!

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.280
What the hell'd you get yourself into?

00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:58.950
I'll be right there!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.700
Come, Ryuu!

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.240
Just a little more!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:15.750
Ryuu!

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:17.760
Sakura?

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.180
What the hell am I doing?

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.770
Am I really gonna follow that divine do-gooder's orders?

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:29.270
But this boy...

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.690
This boy...

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:34.820
Save him, Fortune!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.040
Tittyko?

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:53.670
Ichiko!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.790
Ryuu.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.260
Keita!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.720
What the hell were you doing?

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.970
But the card! The card!

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:13.520
Person. The character for 'person'...

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:17.150
Sakura... Are you insane?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.230
You were lucky this time, but you could've died!

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:26.990
If I hadn't jumped in, you would have, right? Then you'd both have drowned.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.490
Doesn't that apply to you as well?

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.870
Nah, I'd be fine.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.000
What's that mean?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.540
Anyway...

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.590
Thank you.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:42.380
Thank you so much.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.390
I'm sorry I got mad at you, and for everything else.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:50.680
Come on, you thank her too. She saved your life.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:56.520
Thank you, Tittyko!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.900
Ichiko!

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:06.870
Suwano, if you were here, I would ask you.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:14.040
I don't really know myself, but I feel warm inside.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:20.750
You're growing up, Ichiko. You're starting to develop a heart!

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.630
Let's do it right now!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.630
Show me your Fortune, baby!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:32.430
You little bitch! How many of my gadgets are you just gonna break like that?

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:34.480
How much d'you think this shit costs, huh?!

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.480
The company doesn't even cover it!

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:37.600
Shut up!

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.480
Somehow the mere thought of you sucking me dry makes me physically ill!

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.990
That again? What do you mean, "somehow"? You got a problem with me?!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:47.450
Of course! You've been a filthy hobo from the moment I laid eyes on you!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:52.200
Why, you little... I was an idiot for thinking you'd changed in the slightest!

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.250
What do you take this for, a makeover show?!

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:27.960
This week's <i>Nadeshiko ga!</i>

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:31.130
This week, catch me here, here, and here!

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:34.970
I might've appeared in a few more places, but I'm still a very small part of the scree—
